{"id":"math/comb","module":"math","qualname":"comb","name":"comb","kind":"function","parent":null,"signatures":["comb(n, k, /)"],"doc":"Number of ways to choose k items from n items without repetition and without order.\n\nEvaluates to n! / (k! * (n - k)!) when k <= n and evaluates\nto zero when k > n.\n\nAlso called the binomial coefficient because it is equivalent\nto the coefficient of k-th term in polynomial expansion of the\nexpression (1 + x)**n.\n\nRaises ValueError if either of the arguments are negative.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/math.html#math.comb","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":[],"source":null,"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
